<MediaContainer offset="0" totalSize="6" identifier="tv.plex.provider.epg" size="6"><Video art="https://img.static-ottera.com/prod/bbb/media_list/thumbnails/widescreen/3840x2160/around_the_acl_16by9.jpg" guid="plex://movie/6a4eec7f5529ca09280ce508" key="/library/metadata/6a4eec7f5529ca09280ce508" ratingKey="6a4eec7f5529ca09280ce508" summary="ATA 225: Signature #6 Recap: Final Rankings Are Set for Worlds The final Signature event of the season is complete, and the road to the ACL World Championships is officially set. This week on Around The ACL, Jake, Meesh, and Anthony break down all the action from Mesa, including another Signature Doubles title for Tony Smith and Mark Richards and Logan Chamberlain&apos;s Singles championship as he continues one of the strongest stretches of the season. The crew also recaps the Women&apos;s, Seniors, and Juniors divisions, highlighting championship performances from Kamryn Belvin, Sarah Cassidy and Payton Haynes, Jeff Reynolds, Steve Schroeder and Donald Cupp, Zack Aiken, and the junior doubles team of Jack McKinney and Jayce Fleisher. To close out the show, the focus shifts to the updated doubles rankings heading into Worlds. With the regular season complete, the analysts discuss who earned the top spots, which teams have the best momentum entering the biggest event of the year, and which contenders could be poised to make a championship run. The regular season is over. Worlds are next. Join us as we break down everything that happened in Mesa and look ahead to the season&apos;s biggest stage." type="movie" contentRating="M/12" duration="3600000" originallyAvailableAt="2026-07-14T00:00:00Z" requiresConsent="1" skipParent="1" thumb="https://img.static-ottera.com/prod/bbb/media_list/thumbnails/poster/2000x2858/around_the_acl_2by3.jpg" title="Around the ACL" userState="0" year="2026"><Image alt="Around the ACL" type="coverArt" url="https://img.static-ottera.com/prod/bbb/media_list/thumbnails/widescreen/3840x2160/around_the_acl_16by